# Configuration variables, with placeholder values. Copy to .env and fill in.
# Never commit .env — gitleaks blocks it as a pre-commit hook and again in CI.
#
# This app currently reads NO environment variables, and that is the point
# rather than an omission. The MVP declares no network permission and stores
# everything in local SQLite (architecture §1), so there is no endpoint, no
# account, no API key and no telemetry sink to configure. If you ever find a
# variable that needs to live here to make the app talk to something, that is
# a change to the privacy claim in README and PRD §5, not a config chore.
#
# The file is kept rather than deleted because AGENTS.md makes "every new
# configuration variable goes here with a placeholder" a rule, and a rule needs
# somewhere to write to. Its first real entries will be release signing, per
# architecture §9: the keystore and its passwords stay out of git, and only
# paths and placeholders appear here. Illustrative shape, not a live contract:
#
# GAWI_KEYSTORE_PATH=<absolute-path-to-release-keystore>
# GAWI_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=<keystore-password>
# GAWI_KEY_ALIAS=<key-alias>
# GAWI_KEY_PASSWORD=<key-password>
